selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-6+5t \\\\ y=-2-10t \\\\ z=1+2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-6t \\\\ y=-2t \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=5-6t \\\\ y=-10-2t \\\\ z=2+t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=5t \\\\ y=-10t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "227b47dd313aabf3ec3c493d339ad82268d64899097366c5d410a95d978ee0f8" "rationale" "A line through P=(5,-10,2) parallel to v=(-6,-2,1) has r=P+tv for real t. Its components are x=5-6t, y=-10-2t, and z=2+t, exactly original option 1. The stored answer contains identical equations. The original screenshot confirms that the leading brace groups the system, rather than imposing any additional mathematical scope. This is a source-backed derived judgment corroborated by the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grade."}] "usage" {"e-15605" [] "e-15602" [] "e-15604" [] "q-22295" [] "e-15603" []} "basis" 1537 "retractions" [[17592186124755 :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(5,-10, 2)$ and is parallel to $v = ⟨ - 6,-2, 1⟩$."] [17592186124755 :question/answer-fields 17592186121549] [17592186124142 :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n$x = 2 + 2t; y = 5t; z = 1 - t$\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [17592186124142 :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 + 2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1 - t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$."] [17592186124143 :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n$x = 5 - t; y = 3; z = 1$\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line."] [17592186124143 :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 - t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124144 :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1920/Source/Images/fc5afc43c642374b8c9fc33cd5cbe982.png)"] [17592186124144 :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= PQ^(→) \\\\\n&= OQ^(→) - OP^(→) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= p + tv \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 - 2t \\\\ 3 - 3t \\\\ -5 + 4t\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$. And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{x = 3 - 2t; y = 3 - 3t; z =-5 + 4t\n$$"] [17592186124145 :question/problem "Find the parametric equations that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$, where $P(1,-5,3)$ and $Q(0, 4, -4)$."] [17592186124145 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= PQ^(→) \\\\\n&= OQ^(→) - OP^(→) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= p + tv \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 - t \\\\ -5 + 9t \\\\ 3 - 7t\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1]$. Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q$.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{x = 1 - t; y =-5 + 9t; z = 3 - 7t\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121550 17592186121551 17592186121552 17592186121553 17592186121554] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121549 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121549 :answer-field/id] [17592186121549 :answer-field/key] [17592186121549 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
